{"dir":"recv","t":977,"msg":{"id":3,"result":{"data":[{"cwd":"/tmp/codex-fixture-skill-vRYGkV","skills":[{"name":"say-heron","description":"Replies with the word heron and nothing else.","path":"/tmp/codex-fixture-skill-vRYGkV/.agents/skills/say-heron/SKILL.md","scope":"repo","enabled":true,"pluginId":null},{"name":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c:browse-collections","description":"Look inside Spotify content you already have a URI for. Use when the user asks what tracks are on a playlist or album, which episodes a podcast has, the chapters of an audiobook, or details about specific items already shown in the chat, or when a generated playlist's tracks are needed. Covers get_entity (metadata for up to 20 URIs) and get_collection_items (paginated contents, with polling for playlists still being generated). Do not use to discover content from text; use search for that.","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c/4.4.0/skills/browse-collections/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c:build-playlists","description":"Creates and edits Spotify playlists. Use when the user explicitly asks to create, make, or generate a playlist, build one from songs discussed in the chat, or add, remove, rename, redescribe, or make collaborative an existing playlist. Excludes recommendations only, finding existing playlists, saving someone else's playlist, and audiobooks in playlists.","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c/4.4.0/skills/build-playlists/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c:control-playback","description":"Controls Spotify playback, devices, and the queue. Use for play, pause, resume, skip, seek, shuffle, repeat, volume, queueing, switching devices, and questions about the queue, devices, or shuffle and repeat state. Excludes finding content (search-spotify), identifying the current track (now-playing), and library changes (manage-library).","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c/4.4.0/skills/control-playback/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c:manage-library","description":"Save or remove Spotify content in the user's library. Use when the user explicitly asks to save, like, add to library, follow an artist, podcast, or playlist (including one just made with `create_playlist`), or the reverse (unsave, unlike, remove, unfollow) for a track, album, playlist, artist, podcast show, episode, or audiobook. Do not use proactively, on behalf of third parties, or to add tracks to a playlist.","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c/4.4.0/skills/manage-library/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c:now-playing","description":"Tell the user what is playing on their Spotify right now. Use only when the user directly asks what song, track, episode, or audiobook is currently playing on Spotify, or explicitly refers to what is playing now. Not for \"this song\" when a song was just discussed in the chat. Do not call proactively. For play, pause, skip, queue, volume, devices, or shuffle and repeat state, use control-playback.","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c/4.4.0/skills/now-playing/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c:search-spotify","description":"Finds and recommends Spotify music, podcasts, and audiobooks. Use for discovery, mood or activity requests, \"more like X\", known-title lookups, finding existing playlists, listening history, and saved-content queries. Excludes playlist creation or editing, library mutations, playback control, lyrics, concerts, artist bios, and music news.","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c/4.4.0/skills/search-spotify/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"plugin-management:plugin-management","description":"Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access.","path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md","scope":"user","enabled":true,"pluginId":"plugin-management@openai-curated-remote"},{"name":"visualize:visualize","description":"Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspect; create simulations, maps, charts, graphs, and mockups. Use standard tools for static scientific figures.","interface":{"displayName":"Visualize","shortDescription":"Turn ideas and data into interactive visuals","iconSmall":null,"iconLarge":null,"iconSmallUrl":null,"iconLargeUrl":null,"brandColor":null,"defaultPrompt":"Use $visualize to create an interactive visual when a chart, map, diagram, simulation, 3D model, data explorer, or UI preview would make the result easier to understand or adjust."},"path":"/home/user/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/visualize/1.0.89/skills/visualize/SKILL.md","scop